    "formula": "integral_0^2 f(x)d x=2+5=7",
    "text": "Combining the two measurable pieces gives total integral seven. More general nonnegative measurable functions are approached from below by simple functions, and their integrals are defined by the corresponding supremum. This extends the weighted-size idea beyond step-shaped graphs.",
