  {
    "formula": "integral_0^1 x^n d x=frac(1,n+1) arrow.r 0",
    "text": "For x to the n on the unit interval, pointwise convergence to zero holds except at one. The functions are bounded by the integrable function one. Dominated convergence therefore permits passing the limit through the integral, and the single exceptional endpoint contributes nothing.",
